What is the median age of the group?', NULL, $lyceon_json$[{"key":"A","text":"$31$"},{"key":"B","text":"$32.6$"},{"key":"C","text":"$34$"},{"key":"D","text":"$38$"}]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, 'C', NULL, E'With $7$ values listed in order, the median is the $4$th value. Counting from left, the $4$th value is $34$. The value $31$ is the $3$rd value in the list, which would result from miscounting the middle position. The value $32.6$ is approximately the mean of the data set ($\\frac{228}{7} \\approx 32.6$), which confuses mean with median. The value $38$ is the $5$th value, which results from counting from the wrong end or selecting the position after the middle.', $lyceon_json${"A":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"concept_gap"},"B":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"partial_reasoning"},"C":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"D":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"misread_question"}}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, NULL, 'draft', 1, 45, false, $lyceon_json${"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-08-27"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb, $lyceon_json${"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-08-27","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}$lyceon_json$::jsonb);


































- Green roofs are rooftops partially or fully covered with vegetation planted over a waterproof membrane.
- A 2019 study by the Barcelona Institute for Global Health found that green roofs reduce building energy consumption by 23 percent compared to conventional roofs.
- Green roofs absorb up to 79 percent of rainfall, reducing urban stormwater runoff.
- Installation costs for green roofs are approximately 40 percent higher than those for conventional roofs.
- The city of Toronto has required green roofs on new commercial buildings since 2009.', $lyceon_json$[{"key":"A","text":"Green roofs, which cost about 40 percent more than conventional roofs to install, have been required on new commercial buildings in Toronto since 2009."},{"key":"B","text":"Although green roofs cost more to install, a 2019 Barcelona Institute study found they reduce building energy consumption by 23 percent and absorb up to 79 percent of rainfall, significantly mitigating two major environmental concerns."},{"key":"C","text":"Green roofs are rooftops covered with vegetation over a waterproof membrane, and Toronto has required them on new commercial buildings since 2009."},{"key":"D","text":"Since 2009, Toronto has mandated green roofs on new commercial buildings, reflecting a growing trend in sustainable architecture worldwide."}]$lyceon_json$::jsonb, 'B', NULL, E'The goal is to emphasize the environmental benefits of green roofs over traditional roofing. The choice beginning with "Although green roofs cost more" directly addresses two specific environmental advantages — reduced energy consumption and stormwater absorption — while acknowledging the cost difference, making it the most effective option for the stated rhetorical goal. The choice leading with installation costs and the Toronto mandate focuses on expense and policy rather than environmental benefits. The choice describing what green roofs are and mentioning the Toronto requirement provides a basic definition and a policy detail but cites no environmental benefits. The choice about Toronto''s mandate and a "growing trend" introduces an unsupported global claim and omits the specific environmental data from the notes.', $lyceon_json${"A":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"rhetorical_purpose_error"},"B":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"C":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"partial_reasoning"},"D":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"inference_overreach"}}$lyceon_json$: